      "narrative": "Residential prices in Pinal County are essentially flat, with the May 2026 median sale price at $383,849, down 0.3% year over year.[8] Inventory has increased compared with the peak-frenzy years and broader Phoenix data show a balanced market slightly tilted toward buyers, with more predictable pricing and less bidding-war pressure.[7][9] Buyer-seller dynamics reflect this normalization: buyers have more leverage and choice, while sellers face longer marketing times and must price realistically rather than expect rapid appreciation.[7][9] Local demand is supported by Pinal County’s status as Arizona’s fastest-growing county, significant population inflows, and large-scale employers and infrastructure tied to the Phoenix semiconductor and logistics corridor, including recent land trades and a 400 MW battery storage project near these advanced manufacturing hubs.[1][5]",
